today the State Board of Education met  virtually to talk about the return to  school this fall following the pandemic  shut down Kirsten Joyce now joining us  live in studio with a recap of the hours  long meeting here it certainly was Brian  the overall sentiment in today's meeting  was listening to superintendents from  across the state on what happened in  their districts when schools closed and  looking ahead to reopening our schools  in the fall CCSD superintendent dr.  hey-zeus jar shared some staggering  numbers with the board he said out of  the approximate 325 thousand students in  the district teachers have not been able  to make any contact with about 4200  children  another concern jarred discussed is the  Summer Slide combined with what's now  being called the kovat slide when  students simply forget what's already  been taught because they're out of  school as of today the district is still  planning on being back in the classroom  come August 10th health and wellness of  our students and our employees will be  the top priority so I don't have an  answer of what's going to what school is  going to look like because we we don't  know what the guidelines from the CDC as  they'll continue to tell us so I just  wanted it gerrae also told the board  that by June 30th he will have a plan  with dates dealing with the reopening  process for CCSD and as for all those  surveys we all filled out due June 1st  those results will be available June  11th the week from today at the next  board meeting
 

